# [[.Title]]

A Steward plugin for [[.Title]], built with the [Go SDK](https://github.com/treno-dev/steward-sdk/tree/main/go).

## Run

```sh
go mod tidy
steward plugin validate go run .
```

A plugin is started by a runner, not by hand: run directly it says so and exits. Use
`steward plugin validate` to check it, and `steward plugin run --context context.json go run .` to invoke
it. Write logs to standard error.

## Where things are

`main.go` declares the integration (what it needs to connect), each kind of resource and the handlers
Steward calls: `Provision`, `Deprovision`, `GrantAccess`, `RevokeAccess` and `GetAccess`. Handlers take
and return the typed messages of the contract. Leave out the handlers you do not need: Steward offers
only what you implement.

To add a kind of resource, call `integration.Resource("kind", plugin.ResourceOptions{...})` again with its own
inputs, outputs and handlers.

See the [SDK README](https://github.com/treno-dev/steward-sdk/blob/main/go/README.md) for
everything a plugin can declare.
